.TH PAM_PCSC_CR 8 "Apr 2026" PAM_PCSC_CR PAM_PCSC_CR
.SH NAME
pam_pcsc_cr \- Module for challenge-response and NTAG424 card authentication
.SH SYNOPSYS
.B pam_pcsc_cr.so [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a PAM module supporting two authentication backends selectable via the
.B backend=
option.
.PP
.B Legacy backend (default):
Crypto-token based challenge-response authentication.
It only provides authentication component, the rest are stubs.
The module uses the contents of the auth file created with the
.B pam_cr_setup
command and optionally a password provided by the user to construct
a challenge that is sent to the crypto-token over the
.B pcsclite
framework.
.PP
.B NTAG424 backend (backend=ntag424):
NTAG424 DNA NFC card second-factor authentication.
Reads an NFC Forum Type 4 NDEF message from a card over PC/SC,
extracts the NTAG424 SUN URL, verifies the cryptographic signature
using per-user key material from a config file, and enforces
monotonic counter replay protection using a SQLite database.
This backend is intended as a second factor after password authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.B verbose
\- write more error messages to syslog.
.PP
.B noaskpass
\- do not try to ask the user for the challenge password, use empty
string for the password (legacy backend only).
.PP
.B injectauth
\- inject payload as PAM_AUTHTOK for the benefit of subsequent PAM modules
(legacy backend only).
.PP
.B path=<string>
\- template used to find the auth file (legacy backend only).
.PP
.B backend=ntag424
\- select the NTAG424 DNA card second-factor backend.
Requires
.B ntag424_config=
and
.B ntag424_db=
options.
.PP
.B ntag424_config=<path>
\- path to the NTAG424 policy configuration file.
The file maps PAM usernames to allowed cards with key material.
See
.B NTAG424 CONFIG FORMAT
below.
Required when
.B backend=ntag424
is used.
.PP
.B ntag424_db=<path>
\- path to the SQLite database used for replay protection.
The file is created automatically if it does not exist.
Required when
.B backend=ntag424
is used.
.PP
.B ntag424_reader=<substring>
\- select the PC/SC reader whose name contains this substring
(case-sensitive).
If omitted, the first available reader is used.
.PP
.B cue
\- display a "Tap your NFC card on the reader..." prompt via PAM_TEXT_INFO
before waiting for the card, and show the card label, counter, and UID
on successful authentication (NTAG424 backend only).
.PP
.B timeout=<seconds>
\- wait up to this many seconds for a card to appear on the reader
before failing (NTAG424 backend only).
When used with
.B sufficient
in the PAM stack, a timeout falls through to the next module
(e.g. pam_unix password prompt).
Default is 0 (immediate, no wait).
.PP
.B backend:key=value
\- option specific to the crypto-token (legacy backend only).
At present, only Yubikey Neo crypto-token is supported, and the only
option is
.B ykneo:slot=[1|2].
.SH "NTAG424 CONFIG FORMAT"
The NTAG424 policy configuration file uses a strict INI-like format.
Each card is declared in a
.B [card:<id>]
section with four required fields:
.sp
.nf
# Lines beginning with '#' are comments.
# Each card entry:
[card:boltcard-alice]
uid  = 04996c6a926980       # 14 hex chars (7-byte UID)
k1   = 0c3b25d92b38ae443229dd59ad34b85d   # 32 hex chars (AES-128)
k2   = b45775776cb224c75bcde7ca3704e933   # 32 hex chars (AES-128)
user = alice                # PAM username
.fi
.sp
The parser fails closed: unknown keys, missing fields, malformed hex,
or duplicate card IDs cause the config to be rejected entirely.
Multiple cards may be configured in one file.
.SH "MODULE TYPES PROVIDED"
.PP
All module types (\fBaccount\fR,
\fBauth\fR,
\fBpassword\fR
and
\fBsession\fR) are provided, but only \fBauth\fR is not a stub\&.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.PP
PAM_SUCCESS on successful authentication, error indication otherwise.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Legacy YubiKey / HMAC-SHA1 usage:
.sp
.nf
# /etc/pam.d/login
auth   required   pam_pcsc_cr.so injectauth
.fi
.sp
.PP
NTAG424 DNA card as a second factor after password authentication:
.sp
.nf
# /etc/pam.d/login  (or ssh, sudo, etc.)

# 1) Password authentication first
auth   required   pam_unix.so

# 2) NTAG424 NFC card as second factor
auth   required   pam_pcsc_cr.so             \\
         backend=ntag424                      \\
         ntag424_config=/etc/ntag424.conf     \\
         ntag424_db=/var/lib/ntag424/replay.db
.fi
.sp
.PP
With a specific reader substring match:
.sp
.nf
auth   required   pam_pcsc_cr.so  \\
         backend=ntag424           \\
         ntag424_config=/etc/ntag424.conf \\
         ntag424_db=/var/lib/ntag424/replay.db \\
         ntag424_reader=ACR122
.fi
