.BR ntag424_setup "(1)"
.SH NAME
ntag424_setup \- Register NTAG424 DNA NFC cards in the policy config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ntag424_setup
\-u \fIuser\fR \-\-uid \fIhex\fR \-\-k1 \fIhex\fR \-\-k2 \fIhex\fR
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ntag424_setup
registers an NTAG424 DNA NFC card (typically a Bolt Card deployment)
in the policy configuration file used by
.BR pam_pcsc_cr (8).
The card is assumed to already be deployed with known keys.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " user"
PAM username to associate with this card (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-uid " hex"
7-byte card UID as 14 hex characters (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-k1 " hex"
SDM decryption key (K1) as 32 hex characters (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-k2 " hex"
CMAC verification key (K2) as 32 hex characters (required).
.TP
.BI \-c " path"
Path to the policy configuration file.
If omitted, defaults to
.BR /etc/ntag424.conf .
The file is created if it does not exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-id " label"
Card section label in the config file.
If omitted, auto-generated as \fBcard-<user>-<uid>\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing card entry with the same ID.
Without this flag, duplicate card IDs cause an error.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register a card for user alice:
.sp
.nf
ntag424_setup \\
    \-u alice \\
    \-\-uid 04996c6a926980 \\
    \-\-k1  0c3b25d92b38ae443229dd59ad34b85d \\
    \-\-k2  b45775776cb224c75bcde7ca3704e933 \\
    \-c   /etc/ntag424.conf
.fi
.sp
